## 20. Configurable Item Code and Item Description Rule Engine

### 20.1 Core Requirement

Build a fully configurable, database-driven **Item Code Generation Engine** and **Item Description Generation Engine**.

Neither engine may depend on hardcoded category rules or fixed field sequences in frontend or backend source code.

Authorized administrators must be able to create, edit, validate, test, activate, deactivate, version, and roll back rule configurations through the web application.

Changes to rules must take effect through controlled configuration activation without requiring application code changes or redeployment.

The system must distinguish between:
- Draft configuration.
- Validated configuration.
- Active configuration.
- Retired configuration.
- Historical configuration versions used by existing items.

Only authorized users may manage rules. Rule editing, testing, approval, activation, and rollback must be controlled through RBAC and fully audited.

